---
// Mattress cleaning — one of the six "Appliances" leaf pages under the Home
// Cleaning mega-menu. See carpet-and-rug-cleaning.astro for the shared
// reasoning behind this group, and src/data/appliance-services.ts for the
// cluster links.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS. All copy is DRAFTED from the brand foundation
// document. Facts only TLB holds ship as visible [brackets].
//
// ⚠️ THIS IS THE MOST CONSTRAINED PAGE IN THE GROUP, for the same reason the
// mould page is the most constrained on the site. Mattress cleaning is sold
// almost universally on HEALTH FEAR: dust mites, allergens, "10,000 mites in
// your bed", asthma, eczema, bacteria counts, UV sterilisation claims. Every
// competitor page in this category runs some version of it.
//
// THIS PAGE MAKES NO HEALTH CLAIM OF ANY KIND. Not one. It does not say a
// clean mattress improves anyone's sleep, breathing, allergies, skin or
// health. It does not quote a mite count. It does not use the words
// sanitise, sterilise or disinfect. That follows BFD 5.3, which requires
// content touching cleaning methods to avoid advice that could cause harm and
// bars claims the business cannot substantiate, and it follows the precedent
// house-cleaning/mould-removal.astro set deliberately and at length.
//
// The page sells the same service on honest ground instead: a mattress is the
// one thing in the house nobody ever washes, it absorbs sweat and body oil
// for years, and it is worth having done. That is true, checkable and enough.
//
// DO NOT ADD, no matter how well it would convert:
//   - any mite, allergen, bacteria or germ count
//   - "sanitised", "sterilised", "disinfected", "hospital grade"
//   - any claim about sleep quality, asthma, eczema, allergies or health
//   - UV light sterilisation claims, which are especially poorly evidenced
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH:
//   - METHOD. The page describes a low-moisture extraction clean. Confirm
//     that is what TLB does. If TLB uses a dry compound or a UV-and-vacuum
//     machine instead, §4 needs rewriting, and if it is UV, the claims made
//     for it need to stay off this page regardless.
//   - Drying time is the single most important number here, because a damp
//     mattress cannot be slept on that night. Bracketed.
//   - Pricing basis bracketed.
//
// PHOTOGRAPHY: hero is a family B cut-out keyed with scripts/key-cutout.mjs
// against a green screen (a white mattress cannot be keyed off white). See
// src/assets/home_cleaning/appliances/IMAGE-PROMPTS.md.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/sections/SiteHeader.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import Backdrop from '../../components/ui/Backdrop.astro';
import TextBlock from '../../components/sections/TextBlock.astro';
import PathwayCards from '../../components/sections/PathwayCards.astro';
import ServiceBlocks from '../../components/sections/ServiceBlocks.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import TagCloud from '../../components/sections/TagCloud.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/sections/ComparisonTable.astro';
import GoogleReviewSlider from '../../components/sections/GoogleReviewSlider.astro';
import { googleBusinessProfileUrl, googleReviews } from '../../data/googleReviews';
import Faq from '../../components/sections/Faq.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/sections/CallToAction.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/sections/SiteFooter.astro';
import logoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-horizontal.png';
import cardTeamImg from '../../assets/home_cleaning/appliances/cleaner-with-a-caddy-in-a-home-entry-hall.jpg';
import { whoIsInYourHomeCard } from '../../data/whoIsInYourHome';
import footerLogoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-square.png';
import {
  primaryNav,
  headerNav,
  headerSecondaryCta,
  footerServiceLinks,
  footerContact,
  footerCopyright,
  quoteCta,
} from '../../data/navigation';
import { comparisonColumns, comparisonRows } from '../../data/comparison';
import { locationGroups } from '../../data/locations';
import { trustBarCards } from '../../data/trust';
import { otherApplianceServices } from '../../data/appliance-services';
// The five exterior pages, for the cross-sell grid. See the note above
// crossSellItems.
import { outsideServices } from '../../data/outsideYourHome';
import { howItWorks, managedForYou, theLineBody } from '../../data/brand-lines';
import { localBusiness } from '../../data/business';
import { z } from 'astro/zod';
import { getPage } from '../../lib/cms';
import * as section from '../../lib/cms-schemas';
import { sized } from '../../lib/cms-schemas';

const OWN_HREF = '/house-cleaning/mattress-cleaning/';

// In `pageMeta`, on the title and description:
// Title is the SIGNED-OFF workbook text (Keyword Mapping & Metadata, sheet 1
// row 9), verbatim. The old one stopped a single word short of the mapped
// primary `mattress cleaning service` (500/mo).
//
// 🔴 THE DESCRIPTION IS NOT THE APPROVED TEXT, and that is deliberate. The
// signed-off wording is:
//   'Professional mattress cleaning that treats stains, sweat, dust mites and
//    odour. Dry in hours, not days. Book a mattress clean for your home today.'
// It promises a dust-mite treatment. This page refuses to make that claim in
// its own first non-branded FAQ ("we will not make claims about mites or what
// they do"), the DO NOT ADD list at the top of this file bars it outright,
// and BFD 2.4 does not authorise any health or biological claim. Shipping it
// would sell a mite treatment in the search result and withdraw it on
// arrival. mattress-cleaning-copy-rewrite.md flags this as blocking and rules
// that the flag wins over the specification for this one field; the text
// below is that file's proposed replacement, at 147 characters, which keeps
// `professional mattress cleaning` (500/mo) and the approved CTA and drops
// only the claim the page will not make.
//
// FOR THE WORKBOOK OWNER: resolve the meta. Do not soften the FAQ to match it.

// The page's one primary CTA, per BFD 9.5, repeated on every in-page button.
// The approved workbook CTA is the full sentence `Book a mattress clean for
// your home today`, which at 41 characters will not fit a button: per Rule 4
// the sentence goes in the closing block's lead-in and the button takes its
// imperative core. Both come from the same approved text, so the words stay on
// the page either way.
//
// It also resolves a BFD 13.2 conflict: the old `Get an instant quote`
// promised instant pricing on a page whose own pricing block says the honest
// answer is a fast quote. The approved CTA asks for a booking, not a price.
//
// The header keeps the site-wide quoteCta — that is chrome, not this page.
const pageCta = { label: 'Book a mattress clean', href: quoteCta.href };

// §1 Hero. The H1 now carries the mapped primary `mattress cleaning service`
// (500/mo) as an exact contiguous phrase — the plural counts as verbatim and
// reads better in a headline — extended with the region, because `mattress
// cleaning near me` (300/mo) sits behind the term. The old heading is the best
// line on the page and is not cut: it opens the lead, which is the only place
// it survives, because it works by naming two things and the mapped phrase
// belongs to neither half of it.
//
// The subheading is a NEW line. Its extension is the outcome rather than the
// H1's region, and it leads on drying time because that is the page's central
// promise and its main objection — branded FAQ 1 says so in as many words.

// In `definitionBody`, on its first paragraph:
// Opens with the mapped primary as a contiguous phrase — the opening
// paragraph is scored on the first two sentences — and picks up
// `professional mattress cleaning` (500/mo), which appeared nowhere on the
// page before. One clause changed; the rest is untouched.

// §4 Method. Five stages rather than six: there is genuinely less to a
// mattress than to a carpet, and padding it out with a sixth would be
// invented process.
//
// In `methodItems`, on the description of "Low moisture extraction":
// ⚠️ LAUNCH BLOCKER. Confirm this is TLB's actual method. See header.
// In `methodItems`, on the description of "Dried before the bed goes back together":
// ⚠️ The number that matters most on this page.

// The one place this page talks about what it will NOT do. A Callout, not a
// TextBlock, because it is a short aside rather than a chapter — the exact
// distinction SECTIONS.md draws, and the same call the mould page makes for
// its scope note.

// The cross-sell grid. The five interior siblings, then the five "Outside your
// home" pages.
//
// WHY THE EXTERIOR FIVE WERE ADDED. Window, gutter, roof, high pressure and
// exterior house washing link each other correctly but have NO working inbound
// link from anywhere outside their own cluster — the mega-menu's flat URLs for
// them all 404. This module is where they belong, and it is the cheapest fix
// available. See scorecard-before.md for the full finding.
//
// The blurbs and icons come straight from outsideYourHome.ts, which is the
// same data the five exterior pages render in their own "The rest of the
// outside" row, so the wording is consistent site-wide rather than reinvented
// here. Every href is the nested one, never the flat menu guess.
const clusterServices = otherApplianceServices(OWN_HREF);

const crossSellItems = [
  ...clusterServices.map((service) => ({
    icon: 'spray-bottle' as const,
    title: service.label,
    description: service.blurb,
    href: service.href,
  })),
  ...outsideServices.map(({ icon, label, description, href }) => ({
    icon,
    title: label,
    description,
    href,
  })),
];

// In `brandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "Can we sleep in the bed that night?":
// ⚠️ Do not turn the bracket into a number without confirming it.

// §12 Non-branded FAQs.
//
// ⚠️ READ THE FILE HEADER BEFORE EDITING THIS BLOCK. Every question below is
// one that competitors answer with a health claim, and every answer here
// deliberately declines to make one. The first is the hardest: "do you kill
// dust mites" is the single most searched question on this topic and the
// honest answer is that a cleaner is not the right source for it. That answer
// is the page's integrity, and it is worth more than the conversion it costs.
//
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "How much does mattress cleaning cost?":
// ⚠️ BRACKETED ON PURPOSE, same as every sibling.


// CONTENT lives in src/content/pages/house-cleaning/mattress-cleaning.yaml
// and is edited in Pages CMS ("Mattress cleaning", under House cleaning). This
// file owns the layout. The notes above explain why each section says what it
// says; they stay here because Pages CMS rewrites the YAML on save and would
// drop them. The closing block's lead ends with the approved CTA sentence
// ("Book a mattress clean for your home today."), now written into the
// content file.
const page = await getPage(
  'house-cleaning/mattress-cleaning',
  z.object({
    seo: section.seo,
    hero: section.hero,
    // Its background photo sits behind the trust bar and this block together
    // (the Backdrop below), so it cannot be left empty.
    definition: section.textBlock.extend({ backgroundImage: section.backgroundPhoto }),
    // The page's own cards. The "who is in my home" card after them is
    // shared, from Site settings.
    pathways: section.pathwayCards,
    method: section.iconGrid,
    scope: section.callout,
    worthKnowing: section.textBlock,
    // Heading and lead only: the rows are the appliance and outside pages,
    // from the shared cross-link lists (`crossSellItems` above).
    otherServices: section.sectionIntro,
    // The table's columns and rows are the shared comparison table.
    comparison: section.comparisonTable.omit({ columns: true, rows: true }),
    reviews: section.sectionHeading,
    whereWeClean: section.tagCloud,
    // Heading only: the paragraphs under it all come from Brand lines.
    brandLine: section.sectionHeading,
    faq: section.faq,
    nonBrandedFaq: section.faq,
    closingCta: section.callToAction,
  }),
);

const pageMeta = {
  ...page.seo,
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/house-cleaning/mattress-cleaning/',
};

const business = localBusiness({
  description: pageMeta.description,
  areaServed: 'Northern Rivers NSW and Southern Gold Coast QLD',
  sameAs: googleBusinessProfileUrl ? [googleBusinessProfileUrl] : [],
});

const heroImage = page.hero.image && sized(page.hero.image, '1/1');

const ownCards = page.pathways.cards.map((card, i) => ({
  number: i + 1,
  ...card,
  image: sized(card.image, '4/3'),
}));
const pathwayCards = [...ownCards, { ...whoIsInYourHomeCard(cardTeamImg), number: ownCards.length + 1 }];
---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="right"
      imageFit="contain-bottom"
      kicker={page.hero.kicker}
      headingLines={page.hero.headingLines}
      subheading={page.hero.subheading}
      lead={page.hero.lead}
      cta={page.hero.cta ?? pageCta}
      image={heroImage}
    />

    <Backdrop image={page.definition.backgroundImage} tint="muted" opacity={90}>
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock
        theme="muted"
        align="left"
        heading={page.definition.heading}
        body={page.definition.body}
        cta={page.definition.cta}
      />
    </Backdrop>

    <PathwayCards heading={page.pathways.heading} headingAccent={page.pathways.headingAccent} cards={pathwayCards} />

    {/* 🔑 The keyword H2. Third exact instance of `mattress cleaning service`,
        after the H1 and the hero subheading, and the ceiling — the phrase is
        deliberately kept out of the pricing and FAQ headings, which have their
        own jobs. Its extension is method, and "stage by stage" describes the
        five items beneath it accurately. */}
    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="icon-grid"
      heading={page.method.heading}
      lead={page.method.lead}
      items={page.method.items}
      cta={page.method.cta ?? pageCta}
    />

    <Callout tone="note" heading={page.scope.heading} body={page.scope.body} cta={page.scope.cta} />

    <TextBlock
      theme="dark"
      align="left"
      heading={page.worthKnowing.heading}
      body={page.worthKnowing.body}
      cta={page.worthKnowing.cta}
      backgroundImage={page.worthKnowing.backgroundImage}
    />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading={page.otherServices.heading}
      lead={page.otherServices.lead}
      items={crossSellItems}
    />

    <ComparisonTable
      heading={page.comparison.heading}
      cornerLabel={page.comparison.cornerLabel}
      lead={page.comparison.lead}
      columns={comparisonColumns}
      rows={comparisonRows}
      footnote={page.comparison.footnote}
      cta={page.comparison.cta}
    />

    <GoogleReviewSlider heading={page.reviews.heading} reviews={googleReviews} profileUrl={googleBusinessProfileUrl} />

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.whereWeClean.heading}
      subheading={page.whereWeClean.subheading}
      tags={page.whereWeClean.tags}
      groups={locationGroups}
      note={page.whereWeClean.note}
    />

    {/* §1.3 The Line as a section heading, with §1.4 as its standfirst.
        The copy, and the reason this page gets `fast` rather than the other
        variant, both live in data/brand-lines.ts. Change it there, not here.

        `muted`, not `dark`: TagCloud above paints --color-brand and Faq below
        paints --color-surface, so Cream between them keeps the page
        alternating instead of stacking two dark bands.

        No CTA prop. §9.5 wants one primary CTA per page, repeated, and the
        closing CallToAction is directly under the FAQs. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading={page.brandLine.heading}
      body={[managedForYou.oneOff, ...theLineBody.residential, ...howItWorks.general]}
    />

    {/* Renamed: these five are about stripping the bed, drying, old stains,
        frequency and what happens next, so a generic label undersold them. It
        also brings this page into line with the carpet page's "Booking a
        carpet clean". The second heading stays — it carries `mattress
        cleaning` (1,000/mo), the largest term on the row, and is not a fourth
        instance of the mapped primary because it lacks "service". */}
    <Faq heading={page.faq.heading} lead={page.faq.lead} items={page.faq.items} />
    <Faq heading={page.nonBrandedFaq.heading} lead={page.nonBrandedFaq.lead} items={page.nonBrandedFaq.items} />

    <CallToAction
      variant="secondary"
      kicker={page.closingCta.kicker}
      heading={page.closingCta.heading}
      lead={page.closingCta.lead}
      cta={page.closingCta.cta ?? pageCta}
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: footerLogoImg }}
    columns={[
      { title: 'Services', links: footerServiceLinks },
      { title: 'Locations', links: [{ label: 'View all locations', href: '/locations/' }] },
    ]}
    contact={footerContact}
    copyright={footerCopyright}
  />
</Base>
